WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.480 line:88%
Language has form, content, and use.

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:06.230 line:88%
Form is structure: syntax and morphology.

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:08.880 line:88%
Watch what happens to the roles in the sentence,

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:10.780 line:88%
the cat was chased by the dog.

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:13.440 line:88%
The dog is still doing the chasing.

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:16.950 line:88%
Treating the first noun as the actor reverses the

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:17.650 line:88%
meaning.

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:20.110 line:88%
Content concerns words and meanings.

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:22.640 line:88%
A bank can be a building or the side

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:23.340 line:88%
of a river.

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:27.000 line:88%
Teaching the second meaning expands a child's vocabulary beyond

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.760 line:88%
a single familiar association.

00:00:30.156 --> 00:00:33.336 line:88%
Use is pragmatics: communicating for a purpose with another

00:00:33.336 --> 00:00:34.036 line:88%
person.

00:00:34.636 --> 00:00:37.436 line:88%
Imagine a child asks for a red block, but

00:00:37.436 --> 00:00:39.236 line:88%
the partner passes a blue block.

00:00:40.036 --> 00:00:42.596 line:88%
Walking away leaves the breakdown unresolved.

00:00:43.246 --> 00:00:45.786 line:88%
Pointing to the red block and clarifying the request

00:00:45.786 --> 00:00:46.646 line:88%
repairs it.

00:00:47.446 --> 00:00:51.486 line:88%
Children need opportunities to practice initiation, turn taking, and

00:00:51.486 --> 00:00:52.906 line:88%
repair with different partners.

00:00:53.246 --> 00:00:57.946 line:88%
Parent coaching, rich everyday language, and reduced background noise

00:00:57.946 --> 00:00:59.366 line:88%
support those opportunities.

00:01:00.166 --> 00:01:03.226 line:88%
Hearing loss can affect access to conversation and incidental

00:01:03.226 --> 00:01:06.446 line:88%
learning, but a child's profile must be assessed individually.
